    "body": "Closing over a variable from a cpdef method with a generator expression crashed with `AttributeError: 'ClosureScope' object has no attribute 'scope_class'` in `CreateClosureClasses.create_class_from_scope`. Closures inside cpdef functions already report \"closures inside cpdef functions not yet supported\", but the enclosing function never gets a closure class, so the nested generator expression then dereferenced a missing `scope_class`.\n\nThe fix returns early from `create_class_from_scope` when the entries come from an enclosing closure scope that has no `scope_class`. The existing user-facing error is kept and the crash is gone.\n\nTests:\n- Added `tests/errors/e_cdef_genexpr_closure.pyx`, which expects the cpdef closure error for a genexpr closing over a local.\n- Reproduced the crash with the repo sources before the fix and confirmed that only the expected error is reported after it.\n- `tests/errors/e_cdef_closure.pyx` still passes.\n\nGenerated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nTests not run here: Full test suite (only the two targeted error tests were run locally; CI should run the rest), The C++ backend variant of the targeted tests (skipped with --no-cpp because the C++ compiler (msvc) was not found here)\n\nFixes #7196",
    "closed_at": null,
